+
+These defaults can be replaced with entries in the configured MapStruct properties resource:
+
+[source, properties]
+----
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.List=com.example.MyList
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.Map=com.example.MyMap
+----
+
+The default resource is `mapstruct.properties` at the root of the mapping compilation classpath.
+The `mapstruct.configurationFile` annotation processor option selects a different resource by relative path on the same classpath.
+MapStruct does not resolve either resource from the annotation processor's own classloader.
+
+The configured type can be part of the current compilation or generated in a later annotation processing round.
+It must be a publicly accessible concrete class assignable to the configured interface, preserve the interface's unbounded type parameters, and provide a public no-argument constructor that declares no checked exceptions.
+If it also provides a usable public `int` constructor, MapStruct passes the source size as the initial capacity.
+An applicable object factory continues to take precedence over the configured implementation.
+
+Unknown properties, unsupported interfaces, empty values, conflicting duplicate entries, and invalid or unresolved implementation types cause compilation to fail.
+Equal duplicate entries are permitted.
+The configured implementation applies whenever MapStruct constructs that exact supported interface result, including bean properties and stream mappings.
